# Secondary Level (Grades 6–10) — NEB Letter-Grade System Implementation Plan

> **Scope**: Extend the existing Playgroup–Grade 5 Result Management System with Grades 6–10 following the NEB / CDC Letter Grading Directive. Planning only — no code until approved.

---

## 1. Gap Analysis — Existing Models

### Reusable As-Is (Shared Infrastructure)

| Model | Reason |
|-------|--------|
| `User`, `Session`, `PasswordResetToken`, `VerificationToken`, `LoginAttempt` | Auth — grade-agnostic |
| `AuditLog`, `SyncLog` | Audit — grade-agnostic |
| `SyncedStudent`, `SyncedTeacher`, `SyncedSubject` | Already have `gradeLevel`/`class` — handle any grade |
| `AcademicYear` | Year container — no level logic |

### Need Minor Additions

| Model | Change | Reason |
|-------|--------|--------|
| `Exam` | New relations to `Secondary*` models | Term-scoped compilation for 6–10 |
| `ResultStatus` enum | Add `NG_BLOCKED` | Student has ≥1 NG subject |

### Stay Grade 1–5 Only (Untouched)

| Model | Reason |
|-------|--------|
| `GradeConfig` / `GradeScale` | Admin-configurable bands — Secondary uses fixed national scale |
| `EvaluationTemplate` / `StudentEvaluationResult` | Weighted-% evaluations — Secondary uses IN/TH/PR components |
| `SubjectResult` / `FinalResult` / `Marksheet` | Percentage-based aggregation — Secondary uses credit-hour GPA |
| `ReExamSchedule` / `ReExamEnrollment` / `ReExamResult` | Per-evaluation re-exam — not used in Secondary |
| `TeacherSubjectCompilation` / `TeacherSubjectCompilationResult` | 1–5 teacher flow |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Grade 1–5 models are **never modified or deleted**. Secondary gets its own parallel model set.

---

## 2. New Schema Design

### 2.1 Fixed Grade Scale (Seeded, Immutable)

```prisma
model SecondaryGradeScale {
  id         String  @id @default(cuid())
  minPercent Decimal @db.Decimal(5, 2)
  maxPercent Decimal @db.Decimal(5, 2)
  grade      String  // "A+", "A", "B+", "B", "C+", "C", "D", "NG"
  gradePoint Decimal @db.Decimal(3, 2)
  isNG       Boolean @default(false)

  @@unique([minPercent, maxPercent])
  @@map("secondary_grade_scales")
}
```

| min | max | grade | GP | isNG |
|-----|-----|-------|----|------|
| 90 | 100 | A+ | 4.0 | ✗ |
| 80 | 89.99 | A | 3.6 | ✗ |
| 70 | 79.99 | B+ | 3.2 | ✗ |
| 60 | 69.99 | B | 2.8 | ✗ |
| 50 | 59.99 | C+ | 2.4 | ✗ |
| 40 | 49.99 | C | 2.0 | ✗ |
| 35 | 39.99 | D | 1.6 | ✗ |
| 0 | 34.99 | NG | 0.0 | ✓ |

---

### 2.2 Subject Component Configuration

```prisma
enum SecondaryComponentType {
  INTERNAL   // IN — class participation, homework, project
  THEORY     // TH — written exam
  PRACTICAL  // PR — lab/practical (optional per subject)
}

model SecondarySubjectConfig {
  id              String   @id @default(cuid())
  syncedSubjectId String
  academicYearId  String
  gradeLevel      String   // "Grade 6"…"Grade 10"
  creditHours     Int      // totalFullMarks / 25
  isActive        Boolean  @default(true)
  createdAt       DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt       DateTime @updatedAt

  syncedSubject SyncedSubject @relation(fields: [syncedSubjectId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  academicYear  AcademicYear  @relation(fields: [academicYearId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  components    SecondarySubjectComponent[]

  @@unique([syncedSubjectId, academicYearId, gradeLevel])
  @@map("secondary_subject_configs")
}

model SecondarySubjectComponent {
  id              String                 @id @default(cuid())
  subjectConfigId String
  type            SecondaryComponentType
  fullMarks       Decimal                @db.Decimal(6, 2)
  passMarks       Decimal                @db.Decimal(6, 2)
  displayOrder    Int                    @default(0)
  isActive        Boolean                @default(true)
  createdAt       DateTime               @default(now())
  updatedAt       DateTime               @updatedAt

  subjectConfig       SecondarySubjectConfig        @relation(fields: [subjectConfigId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  // For INTERNAL / THEORY — marks entered directly via SecondaryComponentMark
  componentMarks      SecondaryComponentMark[]
  // For PRACTICAL only — sub-headings that sum up to the component total
  practicalHeadings   SecondaryPracticalHeading[]

  @@unique([subjectConfigId, type])
  @@map("secondary_subject_components")
}
```

---

### 2.3 Practical Sub-Headings

Practical marks are **not entered directly** — instead the teacher enters marks per sub-heading, and the system sums them into the PR component total.

```prisma
/// Configurable sub-headings under a PRACTICAL component
/// e.g. Experiment(10), Viva(5), Lab Record(5), Attendance(5) = PR total 25
model SecondaryPracticalHeading {
  id           String  @id @default(cuid())
  componentId  String
  name         String  // "Experiment", "Viva", "Lab Record", "Attendance"
  fullMarks    Decimal @db.Decimal(6, 2)
  displayOrder Int     @default(0)
  isActive     Boolean @default(true)
  createdAt    DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt    DateTime @updatedAt

  component     SecondarySubjectComponent     @relation(fields: [componentId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  headingMarks  SecondaryPracticalHeadingMark[]

  @@unique([componentId, name])
  @@map("secondary_practical_headings")
}

/// Per-student marks for each practical sub-heading
model SecondaryPracticalHeadingMark {
  id              String  @id @default(cuid())
  syncedStudentId String
  headingId       String
  examId          String  // Term exam
  marksObtained   Decimal @db.Decimal(6, 2)
  createdAt       DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt       DateTime @updatedAt

  syncedStudent SyncedStudent             @relation(fields: [syncedStudentId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  heading       SecondaryPracticalHeading  @relation(fields: [headingId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  exam          Exam                      @relation(fields: [examId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  @@unique([syncedStudentId, headingId, examId])
  @@map("secondary_practical_heading_marks")
}
```

**Flow**: Teacher enters marks per heading → system sums → auto-populates `SecondaryComponentMark.marksObtained` for the PR component.

---

### 2.4 Component Mark Entry (IN / TH / PR-computed)

```prisma
/// Per-student per-component marks within a term exam.
/// For PRACTICAL type, marksObtained is auto-summed from heading marks.
model SecondaryComponentMark {
  id              String      @id @default(cuid())
  syncedStudentId String
  componentId     String
  examId          String
  enteredById     String
  marksObtained   Decimal?    @db.Decimal(6, 2) // null if absent
  isAbsent        Boolean     @default(false)
  status          MarksStatus @default(DRAFT)
  submittedAt     DateTime?
  verifiedById    String?
  verifiedAt      DateTime?
  remarks         String?
  createdAt       DateTime    @default(now())
  updatedAt       DateTime    @updatedAt

  syncedStudent SyncedStudent             @relation(fields: [syncedStudentId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  component     SecondarySubjectComponent @relation(fields: [componentId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  exam          Exam                      @relation(fields: [examId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  enteredBy     User                      @relation("SecEnteredBy", fields: [enteredById], references: [id])
  verifiedBy    User?                     @relation("SecVerifiedBy", fields: [verifiedById], references: [id])

  @@unique([syncedStudentId, componentId, examId])
  @@index([examId, status])
  @@map("secondary_component_marks")
}
```

